    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **263 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` acceptance test.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain blocklist by extending `NormalizeOwnerEmail`, the existing step in the `POST /api/owners` (and `PUT /owners/{ownerId}`) pipelines that already validates and normalizes the optional email.\n\nThe change (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/NormalizeOwnerEmail.java`):\n\n- Added a `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` set containing `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, and `guerrillamail.com`.\n- After syntax validation and lower-casing, it extracts the domain (portion after `@`) and, if it's on the blocklist, throws `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2014 the same rejection mechanism the step already uses for malformed addresses. That escalation is handled by `ValidationExceptionHandler`, which returns **400 Bad Request**.\n\nThe comparison is case-insensitive (done against the already-lower-cased value), and this reused the existing error-handling wiring, so no new function class, YAML step, or escalation handler was needed.",
